#
# Per-Dockerfile ignore file for services/persist-api/Dockerfile (BuildKit
# convention: <dockerfile-name>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile FULLY
# REPLACES the root .dockerignore for this build -- it is not merged with
# it). Needed because persist-api's build context is also the repo root
# (see docker-compose.yml), and the root .dockerignore excludes services/
# to keep it out of the *web* image's public root -- which would otherwise
# also strip persist-api's own source (services/persist-api/lib) from its
# own build.
#
# The Dockerfile only COPYs explicit paths (package*.json, server.js, lib/,
# config/email), so nothing listed here can leak into the image regardless --
# this file mostly trims what gets sent to the build daemon as context, for
# faster builds. The one entry that is load-bearing rather than cosmetic is
# the email.config.local.json exclusion below, since config/email IS copied.
.git
node_modules/
analyser/
samples/
archive/
screenshots/
uploads/
shots/
scraps/
site/video-src/
docs/
deploy/certbot/cloudflare-credentials.ini
# A builder's own host override must never be baked into a shared image: it
# names internal recipients and may point at an internal relay. Host-specific
# values reach the container through the environment instead.
config/email/email.config.local.json
*.md
